Description: pvr: map transform feedback counter buffers to their binding
 vkCmdBeginTransformFeedbackEXT and vkCmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT store the
 counter buffers at binding firstCounterBuffer + j, but the init and end
 programs read bindings 0..counterBufferCount-1 and applied counter i to
 buffer group i. The init program loaded all counters with one load from
 the first counter buffer and the end program stored all of them with one
 contiguous store to the first counter buffer. With more than one buffer
 the end store wrote behind the first counter buffer and the other counter
 buffers were neither read nor written, and a non-zero firstCounterBuffer
 used no counter at all.
 .
 Resolve the binding of each buffer group from its varyings and use that
 binding's counter buffer and stride. The init program loads each counter
 with its own 16-byte aligned load and dword select, and the end program
 stores each counter with its own one dword store. A group without a counter
 buffer starts at offset zero and stores nothing. The end program now loads
 the four saved offsets (16 bytes) instead of a count of 8-byte units that
 could exceed its temps.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
